text=Entendo melhor a Configuração ....e coisa esta ficando mais bonita e limpa.%0a%0a'''/opt/ltsp/i386/etc/lts.conf'''%0a[@%0a#        X_MOUSE_PROTOCOL   = "PS/2"%0a#        X_MOUSE_PROTOCOL   = "ImPS/2"%0a#        X_MOUSE_DEVICE     = "/dev/psaux"%0a#%0a# !!! AVISO!!!%0a# Teste de configuracao feita em micro com resolucação de 1280x1024 = isso pode estar prejudicando os teste nos terminais.%0a#%0a# Manual ver:%0a# /opt/ltsp/i386/etc/lts.conf.readme%0a%0a[Default]%0a        SERVER             = 192.168.20.1%0a        XSERVER            = vesa%0a        X_MOUSE_PROTOCOL   = "Microsoft"%0a        X_MOUSE_DEVICE     = "/dev/ttyS0"%0a        X_VERTREFRESH      = "60"%0a        USE_XFS            = N%0a        XkbRules           = all%0a        XkbModel           = abnt2%0a        XkbLayout          = br%0a        SCREEN_01          = startx%0a        SCREEN_02          = shell%0a%0a#mouse com scroll%0a[Scroll]%0a        X_MOUSE_PROTOCOL = ImPS/2%0a        X_MOUSE_BUTTONS  = 5%0a        X_ZAxisMapping   = "4 5"%0a%0a# p180mhz com 32mb ram (tinha 64mb...32mb passo para terminal acima=ws110)%0a# esta lindo com 1024x768 -placa video sis -offboard%0a[ws105.ltsp]%0a       X_COLOR_DEPTH      = 24%0a%0a#****** inico da area pc100+video tridente+32mb ram = drive vesa+800x600  ****%0a#****** tinham 16mb... levar todos ate 32mb ram                           ****%0a%0a[ws110.ltsp]%0a       XSERVER            = vesa%0a%0a[ws111.ltsp]%0a       XSERVER            = vesa%0a%0a# pc100 com realtek8139 - 16mb e 800x600%0a# memoria com paridade%0a# mas levar ate 32mb ram..pois somente com 16mb o X trava%0a[ws112.ltsp]%0a       XSERVER            = vesa%0a%0a# ****** fim da area de pc100 com trident *****%0a#%0a# 55 fica com onda...60 fica onda tambem...conf no setup bios%0a# com 55 ele sobe ate 1152x768 - com 60 nao%0a[ws120.ltsp]%0a       X_VERTREFRESH      = 55%0a       X_MODE_0           = 1024x768%0a%0a@]%0a%0a%0a'''/etc/dhcp3/dhcpd.conf'''%0a[@%0a# RealTek 8139A do 180mhz com 32mb ram (tinha 64mb....32mb foi um p100mhz)%0ahost ws105 {%0a       hardware ethernet     00:E0:7D:80:25:39;%0a       fixed-address         192.168.20.105;%0a       filename              "/lts/vmlinuz-2.6.17.3-ltsp-1";%0a}%0a%0a# Realtek 8029 pc100 usando VESA=800x600 16bits%0ahost ws110 {%0a       hardware ethernet     00:E0:4C:DD:3B:0E;%0a       fixed-address         192.168.20.110;%0a       filename              "/lts/vmlinuz-2.6.17.3-ltsp-1";%0a}%0a%0a# outro pc100 com video=trident - usa VESA fica 800x600%0ahost ws111 {%0a       hardware ethernet     00:80:AD:41:84:31;%0a       fixed-address         192.168.20.111;%0a       filename              "/lts/vmlinuz-2.6.17.3-ltsp-1";%0a}%0a%0a# pc100 com realtek8139 - com 16mb ficou em 800x600%0a# memoria com paridade.%0ahost ws112 {%0a       hardware ethernet     00:E0:7D:81:77:8D;%0a       fixed-address         192.168.20.112;%0a       filename              "/lts/vmlinuz-2.6.17.3-ltsp-1";%0a}%0a%0a# sis onboard - tinha que compartilhar mais memoria no setup para placa de video=1024x768%0ahost ws120 {%0a       hardware ethernet     00:02:44:36:53:D8;%0a       fixed-address         192.168.20.120;%0a       filename              "/lts/vmlinuz-2.6.17.3-ltsp-1";%0a}%0a%0a# 486 de casa - maquina de teste :)%0ahost ws150 {%0a       hardware ethernet     00:08:C7:4B:FC:CD;%0a       fixed-address         192.168.20.150;%0a       option option-128     e4:45:74:68:00:00;  # teclado ps/2%0a       option option-129     "acpi=off";      #teclado ps/2..evita disparo de letras.%0a       filename              "/lts/vmlinuz-2.6.17.3-ltsp-1";%0a}%0a@]%0a%0aCores e Placa de Video Trident PCI\\%0aSe placa de vídeo for trident e micro tiver boa configuração - p200mhz + 32mb ram vai poder trabalhar por padrão com 1024x768 e 16bits=65 mil cores.%0a%0a%0aPara este mesmo terminal, trabalhar com 24bits=16 milhões cores, faça um configuração a parte para maquina e use:\\%0a[@       XSERVER            = vesa@]%0a%0a%0aVer quais resoluções de tela a placa suporta. no Terminal Leve, faça login no X e abra um Terminal e execute:\\%0a[@$xrandr@]%0a%0aMais tarde melhorar/deixar mais limpa o arquivo lts.conf - com o LIKE\\%0aMicros pc100 com placas trident (usando drive vesa) fazer um LIKE para isso.%0a[@%0a# LIKE = section name%0a#     Allow sections to inherit the settings from other sections.%0a#%0a#     added in ltsp 4.0%0a#%0a#     Here is an example where you have several HP Vectras and several Dell%0a#     Dimension PCs that you are using:%0a#%0a#          [Vectra]%0a#              X_MOUSE_DEVICE   = /dev/ttyS0%0a#              X_MOUSE_PROTOCOL = Microsoft%0a#%0a#          [Dimension]%0a#              X_MOUSE_DEVICE   = /dev/psaux%0a#              X_MOUSE_PROTOCOL = IMPS/2%0a#%0a#          [ws001] LIKE = Vectra%0a#%0a#          [ws002] LIKE = Vectra%0a#%0a#          [ws003] LIKE = Vectra%0a#%0a#          [ws004] LIKE = Dimension%0a#%0a#          [ws005]%0a#              LIKE               = Dimension%0a#              PRINTER_0_DEVICE   = /dev/ttyS1%0a#              PRINTER_0_TYPE     = S%0a#%0a#          [ws006] LIKE = Dimension%0a#%0a#     Notice that ws005 inherits from Dimension, but also includes a local%0a#     printer.%0a@]%0a%0a'''Documentação muito boa sobre Video cards\\%0ahttp://wiki.ltsp.org/twiki/bin/view/Ltsp/VideoCards'''
